IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Tests of the rules in dg-core.l4. The expected values are written by hand from the text,
-- not copied from this encoding's output. Each directive is on one line.
--
-- Raw text: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text).

§ `The YMD shim`

-- YMD year month day is Date day month year (the stable build has no YMD of its own).
#ASSERT YMD 2026 10 25 EQUALS Date 25 10 2026
#ASSERT YMD 2024 2 29 EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- Dates made with it compare directly (probe 53 of dialects.md fails on the library YMD of the unstable build, not on this shim).
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 10 25) AT LEAST (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 10 25) AT MOST (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 10 25) GREATER THAN (YMD 2026 10 24)
#ASSERT NOT ((YMD 2026 10 25) LESS THAN (YMD 2026 10 25))
#ASSERT Day (YMD 2026 10 25) MINUS Day (YMD 2026 10 15) EQUALS 10

§ `Units`

-- Section 203(a)(3) prints "66 2/3%". The spelling is (200 DIVIDED BY 3)%, which is exactly 2/3.
#ASSERT (200 DIVIDED BY 3)% EQUALS 2 DIVIDED BY 3
#ASSERT 3 TIMES (1 DIVIDED BY 3) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT 15% EQUALS 0.15

§ `Time limits`

-- Section 213(a): the record date is "not more than 60 nor less than 10 days before the date of such meeting".
-- Meeting on 31 December 2026: the latest record date is 21 December, the earliest is 1 November
-- (December has 31 days: 31 December less 31 days is 30 November, less 29 more is 1 November).
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in days` 10) `before` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 21
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in days` 60) `before` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 11 1

-- Section 164: notice of a sale "at least 1 week before the sale". Sale on 25 October 2026: 18 October.
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in weeks` 1) `before` (YMD 2026 10 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 18
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in weeks` 2) `after` (YMD 2026 10 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 11 8

-- Section 371(b)(1): a certificate "as of a date not earlier than 6 months prior to the filing date".
-- Filing on 15 March 2026: 15 September 2025. Filing on 31 August 2026: 28 February 2026 (the library clamps).
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in months` 6) `before` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 9 15
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in months` 6) `before` (YMD 2026 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

-- Section 212(b): a proxy "shall [not] be voted or acted upon after 3 years from its date".
-- Dated 15 January 2026: 15 January 2029. Dated 29 February 2024: 28 February 2027 (the library clamps).
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in years` 3) `after` (YMD 2026 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2029 1 15
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in years` 3) `after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28

-- Across a year end, and an empty period.
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in days` 10) `after` (YMD 2026 12 25) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 4
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in months` 14) `after` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in days` 0) `after` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT `the date` (`period in years` 1) `before` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1

-- The four constructors set the unit and the count.
#ASSERT (`period in days` 7)'s unit EQUALS `calendar days`
#ASSERT (`period in weeks` 7)'s unit EQUALS `calendar weeks`
#ASSERT (`period in months` 7)'s unit EQUALS `calendar months`
#ASSERT (`period in years` 7)'s unit EQUALS `calendar years`
#ASSERT (`period in years` 7)'s `how many units` EQUALS 7

§ `Kinds of corporation (section 114(d))`

-- A charitable nonstock corporation is a nonprofit nonstock corporation, and a nonprofit nonstock
-- corporation is a nonstock corporation (section 114(d)(1), (3) and (4)). A stock corporation is none of these.
#ASSERT `the kind is a stock corporation` `a stock corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `a stock corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `a stock corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` `a stock corporation`

-- A nonstock corporation with membership interests is nonstock, and not nonprofit (114(d)(3)).
#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a stock corporation` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`
#ASSERT `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`
#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`
#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests`

#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a stock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
#ASSERT `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
#ASSERT `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`

#ASSERT NOT `the kind is a stock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation`
#ASSERT `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation`
#ASSERT `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation`
#ASSERT `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation`

§ `Entities and where they are formed (sections 371(a), 388(a))`

`a limited liability company formed in this State` MEANS
    Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS `a limited liability company`
              , `where formed` IS `this State`

`a stock corporation formed in another State` MEANS
    Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS `a corporation` `a stock corporation`
              , `where formed` IS `another jurisdiction of the United States`

`a statutory trust formed outside the United States` MEANS
    Entity WITH `kind of entity` IS `a statutory trust`
              , `where formed` IS `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`

-- Section 371(a): a foreign corporation is organized under the laws of any jurisdiction other than this State.
#ASSERT `the entity was formed under the laws of this State` `a limited liability company formed in this State`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity was formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` `a limited liability company formed in this State`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity was formed under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction` `a limited liability company formed in this State`

#ASSERT NOT `the entity was formed under the laws of this State` `a stock corporation formed in another State`
#ASSERT `the entity was formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` `a stock corporation formed in another State`
#ASSERT NOT `the entity was formed under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction` `a stock corporation formed in another State`

-- Section 388(a)(1): a "foreign jurisdiction" is outside the United States, every State and territory.
#ASSERT NOT `the entity was formed under the laws of this State` `a statutory trust formed outside the United States`
#ASSERT `the entity was formed under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` `a statutory trust formed outside the United States`
#ASSERT `the entity was formed under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction` `a statutory trust formed outside the United States`

-- A natural person is a kind of entity of its own ("any individual", section 203(c)(6)), distinct from every other kind.
#ASSERT `a natural person` EQUALS `a natural person`
#ASSERT NOT (`a natural person` EQUALS `a limited liability company`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a natural person` EQUALS `a corporation` `a stock corporation`)

-- The kind of a corporation travels inside the kind of entity.
#ASSERT `a stock corporation formed in another State`'s `kind of entity` EQUALS `a corporation` `a stock corporation`
#ASSERT NOT (`a stock corporation formed in another State`'s `kind of entity` EQUALS `a corporation` `a charitable nonstock corporation`)

§ `Votes (sections 216, 242(b), 203(a)(3), 141)`

-- "A majority" is more than half of the base. Nine directors on the whole board: 5 is a majority, 4 is not.
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 5 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 4 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Exactly half is not a majority: 4 of 8 fails, 5 of 8 carries.
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 4 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 5 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Votes need not be whole numbers (fractions of shares): half of 9 is 4.5, so 4.5 fails and 4.6 carries.
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 4.5 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 4.6 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Section 216: a quorum is "no less than 1/3 of the shares entitled to vote": reaching 1/3 is enough.
-- 90 shares entitled to vote: 30 is a third, 29 is less.
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`at least` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 30 90 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`at least` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 29 90 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Section 203(a)(3): "at least 66 2/3% of the outstanding voting stock". Of 300 shares: 200 carries, 199 does not.
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`at least` ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)%) `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 200 300 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`at least` ((200 DIVIDED BY 3)%) `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 199 300 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- All of the base: 100 of 100 carries, 99 of 100 does not.
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`at least` 1 `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`at least` 1 `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) 99 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The constructors set the fields.
#ASSERT (`a majority of` `the votes cast`)'s proportion EQUALS 1 DIVIDED BY 2
#ASSERT (`a majority of` `the votes cast`)'s `must be exceeded`
#ASSERT NOT ((`at least` 1 `of` `the votes cast`)'s `must be exceeded`)
#ASSERT (`a majority of` `the incorporators`)'s `counted against` EQUALS `the incorporators`

-- A base the keel did not list is named in the provision.
#ASSERT (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the members of the governing body"))'s proportion EQUALS 1 DIVIDED BY 2

-- Counts that cannot be a vote are not covered: NOTHING, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 5 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 10 9 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) (0 MINUS 1) 9 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) 1 (0 MINUS 9) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The cast and where a provision is made`

-- The parties and the four places a provision can be made are distinct values.
#ASSERT `the Court of Chancery` EQUALS `the Court of Chancery`
#ASSERT NOT (`a director` EQUALS `an officer`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a receiver` EQUALS `a trustee`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Attorney General` EQUALS `the Secretary of State`)
#ASSERT NOT (`in the certificate of incorporation` EQUALS `in the bylaws`)
#ASSERT `in none of these` EQUALS `in none of these`

-- A party the core did not list is named in the provision, and two spellings are two parties.
#ASSERT `another party named in the provision` "the Division of Corporations" EQUALS `another party named in the provision` "the Division of Corporations"
#ASSERT NOT (`another party named in the provision` "the Division of Corporations" EQUALS `another party named in the provision` "the Register in Chancery")
